{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486024-2e-low-magic","id":1486024,"title":"2e Low-Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-07T21:02:10-07:00","id":1486024,"title":"2e Low-Magic","content":"What 2e options currently exists (any book, not just blue book) for mortal low-magic users equivalent to Second Sight's Thaumaturgists?<br /> <br /> What about 2e options for Antagonist's Cultists?<br /> <br /> I am tangentially aware of a couple options for Low-Magic (Proximi from Mage, Sorcerers from Mummy), but I'm not super familiar with how they compare to the 1e options or what their differences are.<br /> <br /> I ran a 1e campaign many a year ago using both Thaumaturgists (for an ally) and Cultists (for some enemies) and am starting a new one with some of the players from before. I'd like to update the old NPCs and explore 2e's options for magic mortals in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T22:18:39-07:00","id":1486027,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834693-second-sight-into-chronicles-of-darkness\">Here's</a> a relevant question that was asked in the past about Second Sight thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> The purview of Supernatural Merits is arguably bigger in 2e, although it's still not a comprehensive suite but a grab-bag of powers like Medium and Telekinesis.<br /> <br /> Mage's 2e Proximi are individual themed bloodlines and traditions with access to a limited set of supernal spells and a drawback unique to that line of Proximi. They're pretty viable as themed sorcerous traditions that are a little touched by the craft and lack the near-endless spellcasting breadth of the Awakened.<br /> <br /> Mummy's ritual sorcerers are much more circumscribed. While they don't have a literal list of spells they're allowed to learn (thus rendering every other spell inaccessible), any individual sorcerer can only learn a very limited number of rites, and the book provides very few rites unique to ritual sorcerers (as opposed to rituals anyone can technically perform but which ritual sorcerers are just more likely to know how to perform effectively), with those unique rites flavored strongly for specific cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T06:49:18-07:00","id":1486038,"title":"","content":"My group makes heavy use of Second Sight Third Eye, it's a very cool community supp you can get on DriveThruRPG. Updates the old rules to 2E. Also loved Hurt Locker, which Third Eye references fairly frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11932-jerkajerka","name":"jerkajerka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T13:14:10-07:00","id":1486064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jerkajerka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486024-2e-low-magic?p=1486038#post1486038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group makes heavy use of Second Sight Third Eye, it's a very cool community supp you can get on DriveThruRPG. Updates the old rules to 2E. Also loved Hurt Locker, which Third Eye references fairly frequently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything that updates Inferno?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T01:06:16-07:00","id":1486087,"title":"","content":"Geist has ceremonies that anyone can take even if they are maybe too expensive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T08:18:06-07:00","id":1486098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486024-2e-low-magic?p=1486064#post1486064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything that updates Inferno?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not directly nor in terms of Whisperers, Diaboli, Dominions, Testaments, etc, but Mummy's material on fiends addresses their summoning as Open Rites (anyone can summon any demon with the right ritual, though each fiend needs a different Open Rite to summon it), fiends are explicitly referred to alternately with the same name Mage uses for creatures from the Inferno and the Lower Depths, and, well, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1460184-list-of-weird-totems-and-their-effects-on-their-packs?p=1462955#post1462955\">they're different perspectives on the same thing</a>. The gameline focused on eternal servitude is less interested in the processes by which demons from Hell insinuate themselves into the Invisible Realms and subverting human imagination for (the appearance of?) innovation in suffering and damnation, but if you need a monster that has Dread Powers and feeds on suffering whose summoner maybe does not have the best grip on their learned social mores you could do worse than a system for manifesting a monster with various horrifying abilities and a magic system that lets you learn more rituals by losing Integrity in the face of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> By a similar token, Geist's Ceremonies are the hammer and nails by which krewes can enact supernatural change (alongside more prosaic use of krewe actions) and every krewe is a Mystery Cult that provides progressively more potent occult knowledge to its initiates as they climb the ranks and the group develops its lore and Esotery, and Ceremonies include stuff like &quot;lock a ghost into its Anchor&quot; or &quot;summon a ghost from anywhere, even the Underworld, into a body made of maggots,&quot; to say nothing of the story hook where a warped variation of the normal &quot;hold this ghost in place&quot; Ceremony is spreading with the addition of &quot;this also tortures the ghost, and the main person who's learned this version has seized on it as a form of power.&quot; There's also the new take on abmortals, in the Eaters of the Dead, whose exploitation and consumption of ghosts gives them occult power and a less-than-savory vibe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}